          "Others learned the opposite in practice, even if not in words: what I felt, saw or heard in prayer settles the matter. ‘The Lord showed me’ could end any argument, even when what was ‘shown’ sat uneasily with the Bible or with love. Both habits miss something. One risks a faith with no heartbeat; the other risks a faith with no anchor."
