          "The relational gospel answers both. Because our union with God is already given in Christ, we do not need any experience to prove that God loves us or that we belong. That frees us to test calmly, without fear on one side or craving on the other. We can welcome what bears Christ’s fruit and let go of what does not, without condemning the person. And because God is love, we can be sure he does not manipulate, coerce or shame. Whatever leaves people more afraid, more dependent on a leader, or less able to think and choose is not the way he works (2 Tim 1:7)."
